Z||000006||3.8T Fiero GT||10-26-2001||02:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>:ears perk up:<P>unusual bumper for sale? a detail or two please.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR><I><BR>thanks jay, yeah it does look sweet...here the details from my ad:</I><BR><B><BR>Imitation F355 front nose for 86-88 Fiero GT's. Brand new! Bought @: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierofiber/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierofiber/</A>  <BR>Bought from Denny Patton as seen on website. Nice guy, legit too. I brought it into Canada myself as shipping woulda been a killer! <BR>I decided not to use it due to timing/money restraints, asking $500 CDN firm. The fiberglassing is very well done, black, very thick too, unpainted, metal mesh included as well as the faux 3 bars, unpainted to go in the lower nose part, you get both & decide on which u want to install. NO turn signals included, use 95-98 Chrysler Sebring singal light covers, cheap to buy, check website above, can buy at any Chrysler dealership. This WILL need some custom mounting near the mouldings, NOT a direct bolt on but VERY close. <P>I prefer to sell to Canadian buyer, not crazy about shipping (its big but light), hope u can pick it up, it is at Racetech automotive in Toronto's west end now if u wanna see it, sorry no pics</B><P><BR>||||reg||2
